Error [jet.BuildProbeFailed]: Build probe `marks` found no folder holding `jet-ui-no-such-file.a`
 Why: Actions run only after graph validation, in a bubblewrap sandbox with declared inputs, outputs, tools, environment, authority, and probes. Jet does not fall back to ambient execution. A `jet build` run reports this typed build-action failure.
 Fix: Put the folder holding `jet-ui-no-such-file.a` on LIBRARY_PATH
It looked in:
  /usr/local/lib: no `jet-ui-no-such-file.a`
  /usr/lib: no `jet-ui-no-such-file.a`
  /lib: no `jet-ui-no-such-file.a`
  /usr/lib/musl/lib: no `jet-ui-no-such-file.a`
  /usr/local/musl/lib: no `jet-ui-no-such-file.a`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3505
